  "result": "I've written the revised record for `NRS_484B_587_2a` to `record.jsonl`. It hasn't been through the gate yet, so I don't know whether it passes.\n\n**Why `branch_1` failed:** the record mapped three of the listed vehicle classes to legal aggregates (authorized emergency vehicle, tow car, bus). The run's reading leaves all three unresolved, so each one always comes out as unknown. That makes the planned compliant verdict for a transit bus impossible to reach, and those three terms could never affect a decided verdict.\n\n**What changed:** the three classes are now mapped to the road-user class atoms that name them directly. The aggregate atom's own definition says it should not be used when a class has its own atom. Each justification quotes the definition wording that includes the class.\n- **e12 and e13** (authorized emergency vehicle, and one operating under a permit) now use `ru.emergency_vehicle`. The permit can't be seen in a scene, so e13 reads it from the vehicle's emergency class, and the record discloses this as a reading (`status`).\n- **e15** (tow car) now uses `ru.official_vehicle` of kind `tow`. \"Exclusively used in the business of towing\" is read from the tow livery and equipment, also disclosed as a reading (`purpose`).\n- **e17** (public transit motor bus) now uses `ru.transit_bus` on its own.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- The borrowed text for e8 now quotes the full list (a)–(f) word for word, and every element that relies on it repeats that quote.\n- The obligation is reworded so it is unambiguous. The vehicle must not be on the median, every shoulder it overlaps must be an authorized shoulder, and it must overlap either a lane or an authorized shoulder.\n- `branch_1` is now decidable. I added scenarios for:\n  - a tow truck on a signed shoulder (compliant);\n  - an ambulance with no lamps lit on a signed shoulder (compliant), and on an unsigned one (violated);\n  - a transit bus on an unpaved signed shoulder (violated).\n- I removed the proposal for the halt-speed tolerance parameter because it is already in the catalogue.\n\n**Risk:** the run requires a phrase to map to the same atoms everywhere. If another accepted node in this run maps \"authorized emergency vehicle\", \"tow car\" or \"bus\" to the aggregate, validation may flag that conflict.",
